**Not implemented / simplified from the arcade original:**

- **Attract mode** shows a static score table with flapping sprites instead of a scripted gameplay demo.
- Entry-path shapes are approximations (one curved spline per group, single-file spacing) rather than the exact arcade loops; challenging-stage paths are sine loops rather than the per-stage choreographed loops.
- Diving enemies re-enter from the top on a generic curved return path rather than each enemy's unique arcade home path.
- Escort geometry: escorts dive on offset paths near the boss but don't fly in tight formation "wing" positions; escort count for 800/1600 scoring counts escorts still diving at the moment of the kill.
- A freed captive that can't dock (player already dual) simply flies off-screen with no points (as in the arcade, but without the fly-away flourish).
- The captured fighter fires only occasionally and only while its boss is diving; multiple simultaneous captives are allowed but only one tractor beam can run at a time.
- Sound effects are synthesized approximations (the Galaga start tune is a short fanfare, not a note-exact transcription); there is no background music.
- HUD text uses the browser monospace font at native resolution rather than a pixel-font replica; the "1UP" blink and coin/credit wording are simplified.
